            "review_title": "Review at Sushi Hung Hanare",
            "review_text": "PaulSaigon\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam83 contributions\n0\nFake Japanese - Expensive and Nothing Japanese…\nJan 2024 • Family\nExpensive and nothing Japanese…. The owner is Vietnamese… the atmosphere hearing the staff shouting from one floor to another floor…. The fish sashimi cuts are definitely not the ones you will have in a real Japanese restaurant. \nTempura is arriving without the sauce and the ground white cabbage…. But salt in a the corner of the dish…..\nMissing spoon for the salmon eggs…. We had to ask for dishes for eating…. \nThe tempura is from cake flour…. Sweet vanilla taste….. \nGod God God…..\nNothing nothing nothing Japanese…. Even I guess the owner never been in Japan…..\nRead more\nWritten January 6, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
